{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"9bc5e298b29254d7","name":"card_event_hit_the_drop_point","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/CovertOp/events/card_event_hit_the_drop_point","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"HIT THE DROP POINT","text":"When the enemy deploys a unit, suppress it. Can affect a Covert unit.","flavorText":"In preparation for a potential Allied invasion, the German forces started undertaking several measures long before D-Day in June 1944. They started constructing the Atlantic Wall in 1942, a 2,400-mile network of bunkers, pillboxes, mines and landing obstacles along the European coastline. In addition, obstacles like “Rommel's asparagus” (stakes in fields to hinder glider landings) were placed in potential landing fields. Although millions of these wooden poles were placed in fields, their effect on the Allied invasion was inconsequential. Once Allied troops were on the ground, some German units used the “Rommel's asparagus” for defense by cutting them down and using the logs to reinforce their positions.","faction":"Germany","type":"gotcha","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":0,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_hit_the_drop_point","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_hit_the_drop_point_title","SourceString":"HIT THE DROP POINT","LocalizedString":"HIT THE DROP POINT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::gotcha","faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_hit_the_drop_point_text","SourceString":"When the enemy deploys a unit, suppress it. Can affect a Covert unit.","LocalizedString":"When the enemy deploys a unit, suppress it. Can affect a Covert unit."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_event_hit_the_drop_point_history","SourceString":"In preparation for a potential Allied invasion, the German forces started undertaking several measures long before D-Day in June 1944. They started constructing the Atlantic Wall in 1942, a 2,400-mile network of bunkers, pillboxes, mines and landing obstacles along the European coastline. In addition, obstacles like “Rommel's asparagus” (stakes in fields to hinder glider landings) were placed in potential landing fields. Although millions of these wooden poles were placed in fields, their effect on the Allied invasion was inconsequential. Once Allied troops were on the ground, some German units used the “Rommel's asparagus” for defense by cutting them down and using the logs to reinforce their positions.","LocalizedString":"In preparation for a potential Allied invasion, the German forces started undertaking several measures long before D-Day in June 1944. They started constructing the Atlantic Wall in 1942, a 2,400-mile network of bunkers, pillboxes, mines and landing obstacles along the European coastline. In addition, obstacles like “Rommel's asparagus” (stakes in fields to hinder glider landings) were placed in potential landing fields. Although millions of these wooden poles were placed in fields, their effect on the Allied invasion was inconsequential. Once Allied troops were on the ground, some German units used the “Rommel's asparagus” for defense by cutting them down and using the logs to reinforce their positions."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","isReserved":true,"usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCovertCardPlayedFromHand"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Covert","EHelpBubbleTypes::Suppress"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Cues/Class_Specific/War_UI_Class_Specific_Engineer_Socket_Crank_Sequence_2_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/CandidateArtwork/Summer_24/t_hit_the_drop_point.t_hit_the_drop_point","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Rebellion","historyPhoto":{"Asse